## Notes on Arguments and Attributes

- `environment_id`: Changing it forces a new resource.
- `namespace`: Changing it forces a new resource.
- `name`: Changing it forces a new resource.
- `parent_ref.namespace`: Defaults to `s to the route's`.
- `rule.match`: Conditions, any of which matches: `path_type` (`Exact`, `PathPrefix`, `RegularExpression`), `path_value`, `method`, `header { name, type, value }`, `query_param { name, type, value }`.
- `rule.backend_ref`: Backends: `name` (required), `namespace`, `port`, `kind` (default `Service`), `group`, `weight` (default `1`
- `filter.request_header_modifier`: `add { name, value }`, `set { name, value }` and `remove` (list of header names).
- `filter.request_redirect`: `hostname`, `port`, `scheme`, `status_code` (`301` or `302`).

## Import

HTTPRoutes can be imported with `<environment_id>:<namespace>:<name>`; every argument is read back from the cluster:

```shell
terraform import portainer_kubernetes_gateway_http_route.app 4:web:app
```
